<div class="tab-pane fade show active" id="tab-awareness" role="tabpanel">
    <h5 class="text-primary mb-3">
        <i class="mdi mdi-shield-account-outline me-2"></i>User Security Awareness
    </h5>

    <div class="alert alert-info shadow-sm mb-4">
        <i class="mdi mdi-security me-2"></i>
        <strong>Trust Soft Credit (TSC)</strong> implements advanced security features to protect your account and data. Here's what you need to know and apply as a user.
    </div>

    <h6 class="text-secondary fw-bold mt-4">🔒 System-Level Security Features</h6>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>MFA (Multi-Factor Authentication):</strong> Adds a second layer of authentication using your phone or authenticator app.</li>
        <li><strong>Session Management:</strong> Automatically expires sessions after 1 hour of inactivity.</li>
        <li><strong>IP Address Tracking:</strong> Logs all login sessions by IP for auditing and threat detection.</li>
        <li><strong>Password Policy:</strong> Enforces strong passwords and periodic expiration (every 3 months).</li>
        <li><strong>Session Recovery Code:</strong> Secure backup code for emergency logins.</li>
        <li><strong>Account Lockout:</strong> Blocks user after multiple failed login attempts.</li>
        <li><strong>Device Logout:</strong> Admins can force logout of all active devices in case of compromise.</li>
        <li><strong>Blocked Access Control:</strong> Prevents login from unauthorized IPs or blocked branches.</li>
    </ul>

    <h6 class="text-secondary fw-bold mt-4">🛡️ Best Practices to Stay Protected</h6>
    <ul>
        <li>Use a <strong>unique and strong password</strong> for your account — avoid names or birthdays.</li>
        <li><strong>Never share your password</strong> or recovery code with anyone.</li>
        <li><strong>Always enable MFA</strong> — it's the most effective layer against unauthorized access.</li>
        <li><strong>Logout from shared devices</strong> and clear the browser cache.</li>
        <li>Use a <strong>trusted browser</strong> and keep it up to date.</li>
        <li>Don’t store passwords in browsers or on paper.</li>
    </ul>

    <h6 class="text-secondary fw-bold mt-4">🚫 Protect Yourself Against Threats</h6>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Phishing Attacks:</strong> TSC will never ask for your password via email or SMS. Beware of suspicious links.</li>
        <li><strong>Session Hijacking:</strong> Avoid logging in on public Wi-Fi. Use VPNs when working remotely.</li>
        <li><strong>Brute-force Attacks:</strong> Password attempts are monitored. Lockout is enforced after multiple failures.</li>
        <li><strong>Unauthorized Access:</strong> Monitor recent logins and logout of unknown devices immediately.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-4 shadow-sm">
        <i class="mdi mdi-alert-outline me-2"></i>
        <strong>Important:</strong> If you suspect your account has been compromised or you notice unusual activity,
        <span class="text-danger">change your password immediately</span> and report it to your administrator.
    </div>
</div>
